In article <739139341snz@chrism.demon.co.uk>, chris@chrism.demon.co.uk writes...
>Could anyone give a newcomer some advice about how to identify the numerous
>objects found lying around in NetHack, please?  I'm VERY confused about how
> 
>Do the colours of potions and the names of scrolls have some significance?
>ie, if I find a blue potion and find that (for example) it turns me
>invisible, can I assume that all other blue potions will do the same thing?
> 
Let's see... I will try to explain as best as I can here...

During the same game, a potion of the same color will be the
same thing; in fact, using your example, you drank the blue 
potion the first time, and you turned invisible.  The next
time you find that potion, it will be named potion of invisibility
(not blue potion.)  However, the potion that is blue one game
is not the same potion from game to game.  It might be a potion
of extra healing one game and a potion of sickness the next.

The same goes for scrolls.  Once you have found what it is, any
other scrolls you find of the same type will have that name
(for example, let's say that a scroll called YUM YUM is a scroll
of enchant armor.  You discover that after you read it; the next
time you find that same scroll, it will say a scroll of enchant
armor.  But the next game, YUM YUM might be a scroll of destroy
armor!!!

I suppose it boils down to this...the names of the scrolls and
colors of the potions (and the wands and everything else) have
no significance whatsoever except so you can tell them apart
during the course of the game.  I guess it is kind of like
shuffling a card deck; all the cards are there, but you never
know exactly how they will turn up.

As far as how to identify things, there are scrolls of identify
and spellbooks of identify.  When you read a scroll of identify,
it will ask you to list the things you want to identify.
Type the symbol for the things you want to identify and anywhere 
from one item to all of your possessions will be identified.
With the spellbook of identify, after you have transcribed it,
you can cast that spell and the same thing happens as when you
read the scroll of identify.  Other than that, it is truly a
hit or miss thing.

Hope this helped!!!

